@* The filter panel as a sidebar next to the table: every filter of the schema is a section with the same editors as the filter tags (a text field, options with counts, Yes / No / Any, an amount with a slider,
   an issue date with presets and a calendar). A section with a filter on starts expanded and counts its values; Clear filters takes them all off. Each change applies at once and adds a history entry (pnl.f.*).
   Statically rendered the panel is one GET form: type a customer, an amount or a day and press Apply; the operators, options and Yes / No / Any are links that apply at once. *@
<div class="w-full" data-testid="list-panel">
    <LxDataList TItem="Invoice" Label="Invoices with a filter panel" Schema="InvoicePanelData.Schema" Items="InvoiceData.All" UrlKey="pnl">
        <div class="grid items-start gap-4 md:grid-cols-[18rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
            <LxDataListFilterPanel Description="Narrow the invoices by any of these fields." />
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3">
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <LxDataListSearch />
                    <LxDataListResultCount />
                </div>
                <LxDataListFilterTags />
                <LxDataListErrorState />
                <LxDataListTable Caption="Invoices with a filter panel">
                    <LxDataListColumn Field="id" Title="No." Align="DataListAlign.End" />
                    <LxDataListColumn Field="customer" />
                    <LxDataListColumn Field="status" />
                    <LxDataListColumn Field="amount" Align="DataListAlign.End" Format="C2" />
                    <LxDataListColumn Field="issued" Format="d" />
                </LxDataListTable>
                <LxDataListPagination />
            </div>
        </div>
    </LxDataList>
</div>
